## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to encode business rules (privacy budgets), implement deterministic fallbacks, and design practical APIs.

## Key Concepts

- Daily privacy budget accounting per user
- Deterministic fallback scoring when budget is exhausted
- Idempotent endpoints for reproducibility
- Observability of budget usage

## Code Example

```javascript
function scoreOrFallback(userId, budgetRemaining, modelScore) {
  if (budgetRemaining > 0) {
    return { useModel: true, score: modelScore };
  }
  // deterministic heuristic using user hash as seed
  const seed = hash(userId);
  return { useModel: false, score: deterministicRandom(seed) };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Explains how to add observability and robust failure handling in a real API, a common beginner hurdle as systems scale.

## Key Concepts
- Distributed tracing, metrics, circuit breakers
- Idempotency and retry strategies
- Canary rollout and failover testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight circuit-breaker sketch
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold=5, windowMs=60000) { this.failures=0; this.threshold=threshold; this.open=false; }
  recordFailure(){ this.failures++; if(this.failures>this.threshold){ this.open=true; setTimeout(()=>{ this.open=false; this.failures=0; }, 30000);} }
  canProceed(){ return !this.open; }
}
```

